 System

Complete implementation of 20 modules for League of Legends historical
battle data integration with Seraphine project.

Modules:
- M806: Historical Battle Core - data models, schemas, validation (1070 lines)
- M807: LCU API Client - League Client Update API integration (998 lines)
- M808: Match History Collector - batch/stream match data collection (831 lines)
- M809: Player Profile Analyzer - multi-dimensional player profiling (952 lines)
- M810: Champion Statistics Engine - win/pick/ban rates, tier analysis (619 lines)
- M811: Network Capture Layer - Fiddler/mitmproxy integration (861 lines)
- M812: Protocol Decoder - game protocol parsing, packet analysis (738 lines)
- M813: Battle Timeline Reconstructor - event sequence rebuilding (661 lines)
- M814: Team Composition Analyzer - synergy/counter analysis (595 lines)
- M815: Performance Metrics Calculator - KDA, vision, CS metrics (567 lines)
- M816: Historical Pattern Recognition - behavioral pattern detection (509 lines)
- M817: Opponent Scouting System - pre-game enemy analysis (548 lines)
- M818: Real-time Data Bridge - historical+realtime data fusion (522 lines)
- M819: Data Persistence Layer - storage, caching, indexing (513 lines)
- M820: Analytics Dashboard Backend - REST API for analytics (530 lines)
- M821: Replay Parser - .rofl replay file parsing (507 lines)
- M822: Meta Analysis Engine - patch trends, tier lists (503 lines)
- M823: Prediction Model Integration - win probability estimation (512 lines)
- M824: Report Generator - structured analysis reports (526 lines)
- M825: System Orchestrator - module coordination, lifecycle (542 lines)

Total: 13,124 lines across 20 modules, all 500+ lines each.
All modules include _self_test() and pass validation.

